Author: Nathan Krupa <54715560+NathanKrupa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sun Aug 30 09:50:35 2026 -0400

    refactor: satisfy the boy-scout per-file ratchet (#1828)
    
    `ci-light` runs a per-file gaudi ratchet that `make verify` does not: every
    touched .py file must end with strictly fewer findings than origin/staging.
    
    - New tests consolidated into tests/test_smoke_account_state.py; the two
      existing test modules are reverted untouched.
    - tests/smoke/conftest.py reverted: the account-state read is a `smoke_account`
      fixture local to the one test that needs it, so no other smoke's fixture
      chain moves.
    - screenshot_seed: `return_home` takes the User and `require_home_org` takes
      nothing; `permitted_user` and `assert_seed_allowed` are public, so the caller
      passes the production/allowlist refusal in rather than re-asking for it. The
      command's seeded preflight moved to `Command._seed`.
    - Paid down one pre-existing finding in each remaining touched file: named
      `_DETAIL`/`_NOT_FOUND` in apps/accounts/smoke.py, and a `_settle(page)` helper
      collapsing nine `_NETWORKIDLE` references in the pricing smoke.

